<!--
    This id belongs to the PUBLIC store entry (1.0.0, 2026-09-21).

    The beta entry used a7c41e2b9d364f158e0b73a2c65d9f04 (0.1.0–0.1.8). Garmin
    will not promote a beta to a public listing: "If you want to publish your
    app after testing, you must upload it again using a different application
    ID in the app's manifest.xml." So a public release means a new id here and
    a separate store entry — new URL, no carried-over installs or reviews.

    Correction 2026-09-24 (Nico): Connect IQ beta entries are creator-only —
    not a multi-tester system — and they are NOT auto-deleted when the app
    goes public. The id above no longer exists because Nico deleted it
    himself after v1.0.0 shipped; left alone, it would still be there today
    as a standing side channel for testing new builds, entirely separate from
    the public listing. If a beta is wanted again, check the dashboard before
    assuming a fresh id is needed.

    Generate a fresh one with:  uuidgen | tr -d - | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z'

    Watch out: Application.Storage and app settings are keyed per app id, so
    the public build starts with the shipped defaults — Helsinki and Harmaja —
    and a beta tester has to set their place and station again. There is no
    pairing to redo, since the app has no account.
-->
